# This file has to stand on its own. A global gitignore (core.excludesfile) is per-developer
# machine configuration and is not part of a clone, so anything covered only there is invisible
# to whoever set it up and untracked noise for everyone else. See #63.

# macOS
.DS_Store
._*

# Windows — the counterpart to the above, and Qud contributors skew Windows
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor / tooling scratch
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Python: tools/ holds the validators, so running them writes tools/__pycache__/.
# README.md tells contributors to run them, so this is generated on a normal first clone.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Node: the repo's XML formatter (prettier + @prettier/plugin-xml) is dev tooling only.
# It lives at the repo root, never in mod/, so it cannot ship to subscribers.
node_modules/


# Never commit secrets. Nothing here reads a .env today; this is insurance, not a description.
.env

# Qud writes these next to a loaded mod
*.log

# The release asset, which `tools/sync_mod.py --zip` writes to the repository root by default.
# It is a build output and belongs on the GitHub release rather than in git — but the real reason
# it is here is that `--publish` and `--zip` both refuse a dirty working tree, so an untracked zip
# left over from step 7 of docs/RELEASING.md blocks step 6 of the same release. Cutting 2.6.0 hit
# exactly that, between building the asset and installing the publish build.
QudExpandedCommunityEdition-*.zip
